Translation notes on the parts that could easily have gone wrong:[0m[0m
[0m[0m
- [38;5;10mprintf("%s %d\n", strmap[z], strmap[z].value)[0m passes a 16-byte struct by value to a variadic function. Under the SysV AMD64 ABI it occupies two INTEGER eightbytes, so [38;5;10m%s[0m consumes the key pointer and [38;5;10m%d[0m consumes the low half of the second eightbyte (which is [38;5;10mvalue[0m); the explicit trailing [38;5;10mvalue[0m argument is never read. I reproduce that register layout rather than "fixing" the call.[0m[0m
- [38;5;10mstbds_siphash_bytes[0m builds its 32-bit halves with [38;5;10mint[0m arithmetic, so a byte ≥ 0x80 in the top position makes the intermediate negative and the conversion to [38;5;10msize_t[0m sign-extends, corrupting the high 32 bits of [38;5;10mdata[0m. Preserved via explicit [38;5;10mwrapping_shl[0m + [38;5;10mas isize as usize[0m. Same for the [38;5;10mcase 4:[0m fallthrough in the tail switch.[0m[0m
- The wrapped-around probe loop in [38;5;10mstbds_hmput_key[0m omits the [38;5;10mtemp_key[0m store that the first loop does; kept as-is. Likewise the array [38;5;10msh_geti[0m leaks when [38;5;10mshgeti[0m on a NULL map allocates and [38;5;10msh_new_strdup[0m then overwrites it, and the [38;5;10mhash += 2[0m / [38;5;10mhash_seed[0m LCG stepping.[0m[0m
- libc [38;5;10mrealloc[0m/[38;5;10mfree[0m/[38;5;10mprintf[0m/[38;5;10msprintf[0m are called directly (no [38;5;10mlibc[0m crate) so allocation layout, stdio buffering, and integer formatting match. [38;5;10massert[0m is live because the CMake build sets no [38;5;10mNDEBUG[0m.[0m[0m
